Theory Details ->
1. Use Redis to do location update where write>>> read(600K/sec). In this we use geohashing in redis
 instead of quardtree because in quardtree if updates are very freq then everytime that tree would
 need the modification, which would be an expensive process.
2. How to reduce the location writes - handle dynamically at the client level
        a. send update in 10-15sec instead of every 5 sec.
        b. Don't send update if the location is not changed.
3. Two driver should get same request - For this after getting list of available near by drivers, sent request
one by one to those drivers and wait some sec says 5 sec for response and then send to next driver if
its not accepted. This will give issue in case of multiple service instances and all fetch available driver and
send the request to same drivers. Here we would need to store the info that request is sent to this driver and
after a certain waiting time we would need to delete that entry as well. In this situation, we will use redis
(distributed lock) which stores - driverid, requestsent, TTL(to handle deletion).
4 . As we are already using Redis for location. Here we can use dynamodb to store all kinds of data. In Dynamo db
also we can have TTL, So instead of redis will have one more table in db instead of redis.
5. to handle surge request - kafka is used having location id is Partition key